{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Young1967-caseA-equal-ripple-19L",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Multilayer Interference Filters with Narrow Stop Bands,\" Appl. Opt. 6, 297-315 (1967). doi:10.1364/AO.6.000297 - Sec. VI.E p. 305: Eq. (48) n_i/n_0 = 1 - x*sum_{k=1}^{i}(-1)^k I_k with Table I currents (p. 305); case list p. 305; results Table II p. 309 and Fig. 9",
  "Notes": "Non-optimum equal-ripple narrow stop-band (minus) filter designed from a 40-dB-sidelobe Dolph-Chebyshev linear antenna array (first-order theory); 19 quarter-wave layers of graded index, x = 0.4\nSpecification: Stop band centred where every layer is a quarter wave; equal reflection ripples in the passband with 40 dB sidelobe ratio (Table I currents for 20 array elements).\nReported: Table II (p. 309), case A, with theta = layer phase thickness (theta/90 = 1 at stop-band centre, i.e. lambda = reference_nm/(theta/90)): number of layers 19; maximum attenuation 13.59 dB at centre; minimum transmittance 0.044; Vmax 89.41; ripple SWR Vr predicted by Eq. (43) and computed 1.045; centre index ratio 1.49; zeros of reflectance between theta = 0 and 90 deg: 8 (10 expected); equal-ripple fractional bandwidth computed by analysis (Line 15) w = 0.48 (band edges at theta/90 = 0.76 and 1.24, i.e. about 443.5-723.7 nm for reference 550 nm); predicted by Eq. (47) 0.51; first-order nulls bandwidth w1 (Eq. 8, quarter-wave stack of the centre ratio) 0.328, w1a 0.366, w0a 0.352, optimum filter w0 0.400. Fig. 9: response plotted vs theta/90 from 0 to 2 (reflectance ripples below about 0.002 for case A/C).\nNotes: All layers are quarter waves at reference_nm (theta = 90 deg); reference_nm = 550 nm is arbitrary (the paper works in normalised frequency theta/90). End media n_0 = 1 on both sides (the formula returns n_0 after the last interface, since the currents are symmetric), indices are relative to n_0; normal incidence, no dispersion or absorption. Layer i uses index n_i of Eq. (48), layer 1 next to the incident medium; the stack is symmetric (n_i = n_{20-i}), so 10 distinct materials. Recomputed here with a matrix calculation: Vmax = 89.38, centre attenuation 13.59 dB, centre index ratio 1.4875 (Table II Line 9 prints 1.49).\nLayers from Sec. VI.E p. 305: Eq. (48) n_i/n_0 = 1 - x*sum_{k=1}^{i}(-1)^k I_k with Table I currents (p. 305); case list p. 305; results Table II p. 309 and Fig. 9; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours 13.59 dB at the centre; paper 13.59 dB (Table II).",
